  "reply": "I rewrote `parseDuration` in `src/duration.ts`, and `bun test` passes (26 tests, 0 failures). That is the only file I changed, and the `parseDuration` export is unchanged.\n\n- **What it accepts:** one or more nonnegative integer components in strictly descending `h`, `m`, `s`, `ms` order. Whitespace is allowed between components and at both ends.\n- **What it rejects with `RangeError`:** empty or whitespace-only input, duplicate or out-of-order units, signs, fractions, and junk. It matches the whole string, so a partial parse is never accepted.\n- **Overflow:** the total is computed in milliseconds with `BigInt`, so a total above `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` is caught exactly and also throws `RangeError`.\n- **Spacing choice:** your spec didn't cover whitespace between a number and its unit, so `1 h` is rejected. Only whitespace between components and at the ends is allowed.",
